{"title":"Some history of higher education","link":"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/915285209/0/marginalrevolution~Some-history-of-higher-education.html","date":1742619382000,"content":"<blockquote>\r\n<p>To Dr. Damrosch, who has studied academic culture at colleges, the current turmoil was vaguely reminiscent of a 1940s episode at the school now known as Iowa State University.</p>\r\n<p>The school’s economics department — in a paper on economic policy for wartime food production — had proposed replacing butter with margarine, said Dr. Damrosch. The dairy industry and its supporters in the state legislature “went ballistic,” he said, pressuring the school’s president to place the department under receivership.</p>\r\n<p>The move triggered an immediate backlash and mass departure of faculty members.</p>\r\n<p>It might have also played a small role in the reshaping of the higher education landscape: At least six professors fled to Chicago, where they helped build one of the most renowned economics departments in the world.</p>\r\n</blockquote>\r\n<p>Here is <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://www.nytimes.com/2025/03/20/us/columbia-university-receivership-trump.html\" target=\"_blank\">the full NYT piece</a>, mostly about Columbia, via <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://x.com/anecdotal\" target=\"_blank\">Anecdotal</a>.</p>\r\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://marginalrevolution.com/marginalrevolution/2025/03/some-history-of-higher-education.html\">Some history of higher education</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://marginalrevolution.com\">Marginal REVOLUTION</a>.</p>\r\n<img height=\"1\" width=\"1\" src=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/i/915285209/0/marginalrevolution\" />\r\n<div><a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/_/28/915285209/marginalrevolution\"><img height=\"20\" src=\"https: